{#- The workers (founder, 2026-11-17): the one section the revision adds,
    right after Who it's for. Four of the phase 1 workers (the plan's RevOps,
    Finance and Planning, Supply chain, and Performance Analytics packs), each
    with one example request, then how a request moves: Ask, Work, Approve.

    The preview is a static mock, not a screenshot: the app has no worker
    chats or approvals to capture yet, so it is built here in the app's own
    colours and labelled "Product preview", with made-up names and figures.
    The scene is the founder's own (his investor one-pager, 2026-11-12, and
    the plan's demo hero): a commission that came up short, fixed in the
    sales channel. It shows only what the phase 1 plan builds: the desktop's
    rooms, an @mention, a worker's proposal with its checks, the Revenue Ops
    owner's approval (pay changes need it), and every action logged. -#}
      <section class="ent-sec" aria-labelledby="workers-h">
        <p class="ent-eyebrow">The workers</p>
        <h2 class="ent-h" id="workers-h">Expert workers for the jobs you can’t hire for yet.</h2>
        <p class="ent-body">Each worker is set up by OpenShore’s experts for one business function. You message it like a teammate, it does the work with sources, and a person approves every change.</p>

        <ul class="ent-wcards">
          <li class="ent-wcard">
            <h3>Revenue Ops</h3>
            <p class="ent-wcard-ex">Example request</p>
            <p class="ent-wcard-q">“Build Monday’s pipeline review from the CRM and flag deals at risk.”</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ent-wcard">
            <h3>Finance &amp; Planning</h3>
            <p class="ent-wcard-ex">Example request</p>
            <p class="ent-wcard-q">“Roll the forecast forward and explain what changed.”</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ent-wcard">
            <h3>Supply Chain &amp; Logistics</h3>
            <p class="ent-wcard-ex">Example request</p>
            <p class="ent-wcard-q">“Match inventory to open orders and flag shortfalls.”</p>
          </li>
          <li class="ent-wcard">
            <h3>Performance &amp; Analytics</h3>
            <p class="ent-wcard-ex">Example request</p>
            <p class="ent-wcard-q">“Turn last quarter into a board-ready summary, every figure sourced.”</p>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <ol class="ent-steps" aria-label="How a request works">
          <li><span class="ent-step-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><h3>Ask</h3><p>@mention a worker in any chat or project.</p></li>
          <li><span class="ent-step-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><h3>Work</h3><p>It pulls from connected systems and shows its sources.</p></li>
          <li><span class="ent-step-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><h3>Approve</h3><p>Nothing changes until a person signs off, and every action is logged.</p></li>
        </ol>

        <figure class="ent-preview">
